{"kind":"stack","id":"s1","title":"Changing environments and dangers to living things","theme":{"background":"#f4f9f2","foreground":"#1f3b2c","font":"Comic Sans MS, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-q","content":"What is an environment?"},{"type":"button","id":"c1-a","label":"Everything around a living thing, including air, water and land","why":"An environment is all the conditions surrounding a living thing.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"Only the animals that live in one place","why":"Pupils may think of an environment as just the living things in it.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c1-c","label":"Only the plants growing in a garden","why":"Pupils may mix up environment with a single habitat type like a garden.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-t","content":"Environment change"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-e","content":"Environments can change over time because of weather, seasons, people or natural events like floods and fires."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-n","label":"Next Card","why":"","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"Which of these is a natural event that can change an environment?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"A flood","why":"Floods are natural events that can quickly change a habitat.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"A school bell","why":"Pupils may think any human sound changes an environment.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"A bookshelf","why":"Pupils may think any object in a room changes the environment.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"What is a danger to living things when an environment changes?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"Their habitat may be destroyed, so they lose food and shelter","why":"Losing a habitat removes the food and shelter living things need.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"They always grow bigger and stronger","why":"Pupils may think change always helps living things.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-c","label":"They stop needing water","why":"Pupils may think living things stop needing water when conditions change.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-t","content":"Habitat"},{"type":"text","id":"c5-e","content":"A habitat is the place where a living thing naturally lives, with the food, water and shelter it needs."},{"type":"button","id":"c5-n","label":"Next Card","why":"","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-q","content":"A river near your village floods after heavy rain. A family of ducks has nowhere dry to nest. What should the ducks' helpers do first?"},{"type":"button","id":"c6-a","label":"Move the nests to higher, dry ground","why":"","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"Leave them to find their own way","why":"","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"The nests are moved to high ground. The ducks settle and raise their young safely."},{"type":"button","id":"c7-n","label":"Continue","why":"","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-t","content":"The ducks struggle in the rising water and some of their eggs are lost."},{"type":"button","id":"c8-n","label":"Continue","why":"","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"Why is a flood dangerous for ducks that nest near a river?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"Their nests and eggs can be washed away","why":"Rising water can sweep away nests on low ground.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"Their feathers become too bright","why":"Pupils may think floods change animal appearance.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-c","label":"The river becomes too cold to swim in","why":"Pupils may think only temperature matters in floods.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"Which change in an environment could harm a pond's living things?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"Water pollution from waste","why":"Pollution makes water unsafe for plants and animals.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"Fresh rain falling into the pond","why":"Pupils may think rain always harms a pond.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"Sunshine warming the surface","why":"Pupils may think sunshine always harms living things.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-h","content":"You finished the lesson on changing environments!"},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"Well done. You now know how environments change and how those changes can put living things in danger."}],"actions":[]}}
